From: Prism <prism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:00:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [Win] Option to build with line tables only

WEBKIT_MSVC_LINE_TABLES_ONLY=ON keeps call stacks symbolized (functions and
lines) without full debug info, so the build directory is a fraction of the
size. Prism's CI saves its build directory between stages.
---
 Source/cmake/OptionsMSVC.cmake | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/cmake/OptionsMSVC.cmake b/Source/cmake/OptionsMSVC.cmake
index 4b4d676b3..d3cb6d841 100644
--- a/Source/cmake/OptionsMSVC.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/OptionsMSVC.cmake
@@ -75,8 +75,14 @@ endfunction()
 # Use AT&T syntax for inline asm
 MSVC_ADD_COMPILE_OPTIONS(/clang:-masm=att)
 
-# Create pdb files for debugging purposes, also for Release builds
-MSVC_ADD_COMPILE_OPTIONS(/Zi /GS)
+# Create pdb files for debugging purposes, also for Release builds.
+# WEBKIT_MSVC_LINE_TABLES_ONLY keeps only line tables (call stacks still
+# resolve to functions and lines), which makes the objects much smaller.
+if (WEBKIT_MSVC_LINE_TABLES_ONLY)
+    MSVC_ADD_COMPILE_OPTIONS(/Zi /clang:-gline-tables-only /GS)
+else ()
+    MSVC_ADD_COMPILE_OPTIONS(/Zi /GS)
+endif ()
 
 # Disable ICF (identical code folding) optimization,
 # as it makes it unsafe to pointer-compare functions with identical definitions.
